      "source": "103003",
      "raw": "Demon of Knowledge ~ is a Daedric Prince whose sphere is forbidden knowledge and the ‘scrying of the cides of Pare, of the past and fucure as read in the stars and heavens, and in whose dominion are the treasures of knowledge and memory’. Mora has been called the wisesr of the Daedric Princes, with a mind as old as Tamriel and a body of slime, though he describes himself as ‘The riddle unsolveable, The door unopenable, The book unreadable. The question unanswerable.’ Unlike most Princes, Hermaeus Mora does not cake on a humanoid form, manifesting insread as varied, grotesque assemblages of eyes, tenracles, and claws, or a featureless purple vortex known as the Wretched Abyss. He is also known as Herma- Mora, The Woodland Man - Ancient Armoran demon who, at one time, nearly seduced the Nords into becoming Aldmer. Most Ysgramor myths are about escaping the wiles of old Herma-Mora. He is vaguely related to the cule origins of the Morag Tong ~ Foresters Guild, if only by association with Mephala.",
