      "source": "103055",
      "raw": "God of Curses ~ is a Daedric Prince whose sphere is ‘the patronage of the spurned and ostracized, the keeper of the Sworn Oach, and the Bloody Curse’, as well as conflict, battle, broken promises, and anguish. Malacach has been described as a ‘weak but vengeful’ Daedra, and he fittingly is not recognized as a Daedra Lord by his peers. The Prince rules over a realm of Oblivion known as the Ashpict., Malacarh was created when Boethiah ate the Altmeri ancestor spirit, Trinimac, alchough Malacath himself says thac this tale is far too ‘literal minded’. Additionally, Trinimac’s most devout Glven followers were transformed ince the Orsimer. However, some Orsimer cling to the belief thar Trinimac still exists and Malacarh is a separate entiry. Goblinkind worships the \"Blue God', whom they venerate with sacred idals of Malacath, painted blue. Associated with Horde King Malooc, an enemy god of the Ra Gada, Malacath is usually venerated by Orsimers.",
